<%# Shown when ticking "time-critical" would buy the caregiver nothing. The
    early alert only ever fires from a reminder call's webhook, so saying so
    beats letting somebody tick it for a dose that matters and believe they
    have bought fifty minutes they have not.

    Rendered from both the new and edit reminder forms, which carried
    byte-identical copies of this until review caught the same wording problem
    in both of them at once. %>
<% reason = missing_call_reason_for_alert(care_receiver) %>
<% if reason %>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-amber-800">
    <strong>This won't do anything yet.</strong>
    <%= reason %>, and the early alert comes from an unanswered call. You'll
    still hear when a reminder is missed, an hour after it was due.
  </p>
<% end %>
